{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation evidence (read-only production probe, 2026-08-09): queried Gerrit events-log with the checkout credential and inspected only event structure/approval transitions. Found 551 LLM-Review approval events: all were `comment-added`, and all carried both `patchSet.revision` and `patchSet.ref`. Shapes included 430 value-0 events, 114 0→+1 events, 4 0→-1 events, 2 initial +1 events, 1 initial -1 event, and 1 -1→+1 event. This proves a review-label/comment write emits the fresh patchset-bearing event needed to re-admit an old rerun target after the persisted cursor. No ticket/change content or credentials were logged. The revised plan also verifies the post-reset no-nonzero-vote state before acknowledging, so an admin/concurrent vote cannot create a falsely durable acceptance."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786337562446551001,"uuid":"942fe0a1-f816-401a-a5e6-92a9d1e2ec4f"}